From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] rtl8822ce: pass cfg80211 its own external_auth_params type

rtw_cfg80211_external_auth_request() builds the request in the driver's
private struct rtw_external_auth_params and casts it to struct
cfg80211_external_auth_params. The private copy predates the pmkid
pointer (Linux 5.1) and mld_addr (Linux 6.3): it is 68 bytes, the kernel
type is 72 bytes on 64-bit, and mld_addr sits at offset 64. cfg80211
therefore reads the last two bytes of mld_addr past the end of the
driver's object. With the stack protector those bytes are the canary,
whose low byte is always 0 and the next random, so the address is
non-zero (observed: 00:00:00:00:00:70) and nl80211 forwards it to
userspace as NL80211_ATTR_MLD_ADDR.

wpa_supplicant 2.11 and later takes that address as the SAE peer, so the
SAE frames go to a station that does not exist and WPA3 association
fails every time, except when that canary byte happens to be 0. The read
is also a stack out-of-bounds access that leaks a canary byte.

Build the request in the kernel's own type, as rtl8852ce already does.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Benjamin Kelenyi <benjamin@wendy.sh>
---
 .../rtl8822ce/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c   | 26 +++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
index 4790dd8..ee465c3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtl8822ce/os_dep/linux/ioctl_cfg80211.c
@@ -7204,7 +7204,6 @@ static int cfg80211_rtw_set_monitor_channel(struct wiphy *wiphy
 
 void rtw_cfg80211_external_auth_request(_adapter *padapter, union recv_frame *rframe)
 {
-	struct rtw_external_auth_params params;
 	struct wireless_dev *wdev = padapter->rtw_wdev;
 	struct net_device *netdev = wdev_to_ndev(wdev);
 	struct mlme_ext_priv *pmlmeext = &(padapter->mlmeextpriv);
@@ -7220,16 +7219,21 @@ void rtw_cfg80211_external_auth_request(_adapter *padapter, union recv_frame *rf
 
 #if (KERNEL_VERSION(4, 17, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE) \
     || defined(CONFIG_KERNEL_PATCH_EXTERNAL_AUTH)
-	params.action = EXTERNAL_AUTH_START;
-	_rtw_memcpy(params.bssid, get_my_bssid(&pmlmeinfo->network), ETH_ALEN);
-	params.ssid.ssid_len = pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.SsidLength;
-	_rtw_memcpy(params.ssid.ssid, pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.Ssid,
-		pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.SsidLength);
-	params.key_mgmt_suite = 0x8ac0f00;
-
-	RTW_INFO("external auth: use kernel API: cfg80211_external_auth_request()\n");
-	cfg80211_external_auth_request(netdev,
-		(struct cfg80211_external_auth_params *)&params, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	{
+		/* Not struct rtw_external_auth_params: that copy is shorter than
+		 * the kernel's type, so cfg80211 would read mld_addr past its end. */
+		struct cfg80211_external_auth_params params = {0};
+
+		params.action = NL80211_EXTERNAL_AUTH_START;
+		_rtw_memcpy(params.bssid, get_my_bssid(&pmlmeinfo->network), ETH_ALEN);
+		params.ssid.ssid_len = pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.SsidLength;
+		_rtw_memcpy(params.ssid.ssid, pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.Ssid,
+			pmlmeinfo->network.Ssid.SsidLength);
+		params.key_mgmt_suite = 0x8ac0f00;
+
+		RTW_INFO("external auth: use kernel API: cfg80211_external_auth_request()\n");
+		cfg80211_external_auth_request(netdev, &params, GFP_ATOMIC);
+	}
 #elif (KERNEL_VERSION(2, 6, 37) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
 	set_frame_sub_type(frame, WIFI_AUTH);
 
-- 
